description: React, Next.js, styling, and Tailwind CSS v4 conventions.
globs: **/*.tsx, src/app/globals.css
alwaysApply: false
---

# UI & Components

- **Components**: Always use Arrow Functions.
- **Exports**: Use `default export` ONLY for Next.js App Router special files (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx`, `global-error.tsx`, `template.tsx`, `default.tsx`). Use `named export` for all regular components.
- **App Router**: Separate Server/Client Components. Use `"use client"` strictly only when necessary.
- **A11y**: Use semantic HTML. Use `<button>`/`<a>` for clickables, not `<div>`.

# Tailwind CSS

- Sort classes using `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss`.
- Use `rem` by default. Use `px` ONLY for `max-width` and `border` thickness.
- Merge class names using the project's `cn()` utility.
- Never concatenate Tailwind classes using template literals or string arrays.

# Component Variants

- Components with variants (e.g. Button, Badge, Input, Modal) MUST use `class-variance-authority (cva)`.
- Define variants with `cva()`.
- Define default values with `defaultVariants`.
- Use `VariantProps<typeof variants>` to infer variant types.
- Always merge external `className` last using `cn()`.

# Design Tokens (globals.css)

- ALWAYS prioritize `globals.css` tokens.
- NEVER use arbitrary values (e.g. `bg-[#ff0000]`) inside components.
- Colors must use the `--color-{name}-{shade}` format.
- If a required semantic color does not exist, define it in `globals.css` before using it.
- Typography must use predefined classes such as `text-{size}-{weight}`.
- Do not combine multiple typography utilities.

# Component Design

- Every reusable component must support `className`.
- Keep components presentation-only.
- Never include API calls, React Query, or business logic.
- Never hardcode domain-specific values.
- Prefer reusable props over duplicated implementations.

# Storybook

- Every reusable component should include a Storybook story.
- Stories should cover every supported variant and major state.

# Figma

- Analyze the relevant Figma design before implementation whenever available.
- Reuse existing design tokens whenever possible.
- Do not introduce new visual styles without confirming they are not already defined in the design system.

# Fonts & Assets

- **Pretendard** is the ONLY font.
- Do not apply custom letter-spacing.
- Use SVGR for vector icons.
- Use static SVG files for logos and banners.
